     <h1 class="title" title="Munnar Hill Station">Munnar</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">

<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/south-india-hill-stations/Munnar-hill-station.jpg" title="Munnar hill station" alt="Munnar hill station, hill stations in india, south india hill stations, Munnar" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location: Eastern part of Kerala</b><br />
<b>Area:</b> 137sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Gift of Forest<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 5000m above sea level.<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 15&#176;C to 25&#176;C, Winter 0&#176;C to 10&#176;C.<br />
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b> September to May.</p>
<p>Munnar, <b>Idukki District</b>,  Kerala is <b>God&#39;s own country</b> is the crown <b>jewel of the Western Ghat</b>. Munnar is situated at the confluence of three rivers Nallathani say, and kundala Muthirapuzha. Backwaters and lush green tea gardens are a wonder. These together with the cool climate make it ideal for honeymooners</p>
<h3>Attractions of Munnar</h3>
<p>Farm co-owned a Mattupetty India and Switzerland, the dam and the lake, where you can swim, boat, are attractions for everyone. <b>Ervikulam National Park</b> is located 15 km from Munnar, which hosts a huge population of Nilgiri Tahr. It is also <b>Anamudi peak</b>. <b>Devikulam</b> is a place for only 7 km from Munnar and solace and recreation. This site offers picnic <b>fishing lake</b> is famous <b>Sita Devi</b> and attract tourists and local Devikulam. Numerous natural caves full of ancient paintings of forcing everyone to visit atleast once Marayoor. <b>Nyaymakad</b> is a <b>paradise for trekkers</b> and refreshes the views of the surrounding area.</p>


